TY  - GEN
AU  - Ridham Patel
TI  - Capturing High Frequency Features Using HF-Boost Based Spectrally Adaptive Physics-Informed Neural Networks
PY  - 2026
T2  - ASCML 2026
UR  - https://ridhamp4.github.io/papers/papers/capturing-high-frequency-features-using-hf-boost-based-spectrally-adapti-2/
AB  - Neural networks are known to exhibit spectral bias, often learning low-frequency components faster than high-frequency components. This limitation is especially important in scientific machine learning, where sharp gradients, boundary layers, shocks, and oscillatory solutions may carry substantial high-frequency content. We propose HF-Boost, a spectrally adaptive physics-informed neural network (PINN) training strategy that monitors the PDE residual in Fourier bands and increases the PDE-loss weight when high-frequency residual energy is prominent. On Burgers' equation and additional benchmark PDEs, the method improves high-frequency-region accuracy relative to fixed-weight PINN baselines.
ER  - 
